{"type":"text","timestamp":1790444217337,"sessionID":"ses_f213b1b20ffebbHhMDFsTGo0qE","part":{"id":"prt_0decaa3e8001REhyV79gGHPdSW","messageID":"msg_0deca4ff90016r9vjNFMpA5Yzk","sessionID":"ses_f213b1b20ffebbHhMDFsTGo0qE","type":"text","text":"Maximum steps for this agent have been reached. Tools are disabled until next user input.\n\n## Summary of work accomplished\n\nThe task is **fully implemented**. The file `/workspace/scripts/projectile.gd` was rewritten to:\n\n1. **Advance the quest on enemy overlap** — The projectile connects its `area_entered` signal in `_ready()` to `_on_area_entered()`. When the colliding area is in the `\"enemy\"` group, it calls `QuestManager.progress_quest(\"shoot_em_up\", \"kill_step\")` using the autoloaded QuestManager singleton and the actual quest ID / step ID defined in `quests/shoot_em_up_quest.tres`.\n\n2. **Queue-free after the hit** — Immediately after progressing the quest, the projectile calls `queue_free()`.\n\n3. **Off-screen removal (50 px margin)** — In `_physics_process()`, after moving, the projectile checks its position against the viewport rect expanded by 50 pixels on every side (`y < -50`, `y > height + 50`, `x < -50`, `x > width + 50`) and calls `queue_free()` when outside.\n\n## Verification performed\n\n- Headless Godot tests confirmed the quest's `kill_step` `collected` counter increments from 0 → 1 when `_on_area_entered(enemy)` fires, and the projectile is queued for deletion after the hit.\n- Off-screen tests confirmed projectiles positioned 60+ pixels beyond any edge are queued for deletion.\n- The scene runs without script errors under Godot 4.4.1 headless mode.\n- A temporary test script (`test_verify.gd`) created during debugging was removed from `/workspace`.\n\n## Remaining tasks\n\nNone — the implementation is complete and verified at runtime. The only artifacts remaining from verification are throwaway scripts in `/tmp` (outside the project), which do not affect the project.\n\n## Recommendations\n\nNone required. If desired, one could add a runtime label update in `main.gd` to display quest progress on the `QuestProgress` label, but that was outside the scope of this task.","time":{"start":1790444217320,"end":1790444217322},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"resp_95e7179295314e57ae22294c4d43f12d_msg"}}}}
